#!build/cubical
-- lib/etym.cub — any English text returned with the etymology of its words (Avik, 2026-11-14; the
-- program of tools/etym.py, 2026-11-16, in hyperactive): each word followed by ⟨its immediate origin and
-- that origin's sense ← its deepest root and that root's sense⟩, then each word's first sense, its full
-- etymology and the chain of origins followed back to the root. Source: English Wiktionary (snapshot
-- 2026-10-01) in the StarDict files of xxyzz/wiktionary_stardict (release 20261029; CC BY-SA 4.0), each
-- origin followed into its own language's entries; GCIDE (Webster 1913) for a word Wiktionary lacks.
-- Fetched once into build/ (curl, tar and zstd, gzip: programs the machine runs, not code of the work);
-- each language's index (build/etym/LANG.index) is its StarDict index as lines `HEAD TAB OFFSET TAB
-- SIZE`, the synonyms (word forms) as `FORM TAB #LINE`, cut once by this program as the language is first
-- needed; a word is found by grep and its article cut out of the dictionary by dd.
import "host.cub"

